{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"6489acab0af75f9b4f54867ec32ee5d537f513e63876aef7cdb557231ddafe78","digest":{"component_or_area":"GitHub Actions CI workflow","key_entities":[".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml",".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml","docs/coverage.md","tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py","pytest","--cov","--cov-report","matrix.os","macos-latest"],"problem_keywords":["CI performance","coverage collection overhead","macOS runner contention","pytest","wall-clock time"],"propositions":["The macOS pytest job default-suite step consumes 15.4m of an 18.6m total runtime due to coverage collection overhead, while three ubuntu cells enforce the same 70% coverage floor.","macOS runner concurrency is scarce and causes 6.7–8.4m queue delays for dependent changes, making job duration doubly valuable as both critical path and scarce resource holder.","Coverage flags must be conditional per-OS matrix in the test job default-suite step so macOS runs without --cov and --cov-report while ubuntu cells retain them.","The test selection and pass count must remain identical across platforms; only the tracing overhead is removed."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787887932418097001,"uuid":"8777c22e-02ef-45b3-aefb-c91ecbba07e1"}